  "projectUrl": "https://github.com/treealarm/OnvifLib",
  "published": "2026-10-12T15:26:42.163Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "1.2.0: Cameras that do not answer GetServices (ONVIF 1.x/2.0) are now reached through GetCapabilities (Camera.UsedCapabilitiesFallback says which). Events: GetEventProperties, GetServiceCapabilities, SetSynchronizationPoint and topic filters (EventService1.SetTopicFilterAsync). Imaging: IR cut filter, exposure, white balance, WDR, backlight compensation and focus configuration, plus focus moves and status. PTZ: home position, nodes, auxiliary commands and a speed for GotoPreset. Device administration on Camera: users, date/time mode and time zone, network interfaces, DNS, NTP, hostname, protocols, gateway and discovery scopes. Media: OSD and video source configurations. Profile G: recording options, creating recordings, tracks and jobs, job configuration and state, and FindEvents. OnvifImagingSettings, OnvifImagingOptions and OnvifProfileInfo gained optional trailing members — source-compatible, but consumers must recompile. Fixes: Media1 profiles now report the physical video source in VideoSourceToken (it was the configuration token, which Imaging rejects on cameras where the two differ; the configuration token is now VideoSourceConfigToken); SetTimeAsync keeps the camera time zone and DST flag instead of clearing them.",
